{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show a clear upswing, the model under-forecasts most of the next ~1–20 days by roughly +0.5 to +2.0 €/t; apply an upward level shift early in the horizon.",
    "Hump timing/shape error: the model tends to place the local peak too early and/or too high, then fades too quickly; keep the mid-horizon (≈days 10–20) elevated for longer and reduce the speed of the subsequent decline.",
    "Over-correction on downturns at longer horizons: beyond ~day 20 the model often drops below realized prices (sometimes by several €/t) after forecasting a sharp selloff; dampen late-horizon negative slopes and pull forecasts back toward the recent mean.",
    "Mean-reversion strength is too high: after a run-up, the model reverts to lower levels faster than reality; reduce mean-reversion parameter (or blend more trend persistence) especially after breakout weeks.",
    "Event/spike handling: after sharp upward moves, the model can overshoot the peak (days ~12–18) but still underpredict the overall plateau; cap peak amplitude slightly while lifting the surrounding days (broader, flatter peak)."
  ]
}
